  "notes": "Waiver filing, cash basis (Exhibit A). General and Street columns governmental; Enterprise Fund column business-type (beginning 5,733 + State Receipts: Other 31,699 - Capital Improvements 33,643 = 3,789). Mixed rows (State Receipts: Other, Capital Improvements) split by fund column. Solid Waste 4,912 and Water 6,315 disbursements and Debt Service 3,232 are printed in the General Fund column, so kept governmental per column. Governmental cash = line 3/28 subtotals (net cash + Street investments), roll-forward 54,299 + 75,698 - 39,053 = 90,944. Capital Improvements has no printed function, so labelled 'Capital Outlay'. Pages 2 and 4 (pages 1a/2a) are blank continuation columns. Transfer General to Street 2,430 (schedule p5). Outstanding NDEE lagoon debt 113,200 (p5) is not on the cash statement, so no liabilities. Investments: CD 5,138 (Street Fund). County treasurer balances 20.14 / 86.35 printed below the statement, not in the roll-forward. No other detail schedules; detail is per fund column from Exhibit A. Read pages 1-5 of 5"
}
